# AI Starter Kit - Environment Variables Example
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development

# =============================================================================
# CONVEX (Auto-generated by `bunx convex dev`)
# =============================================================================

# Your Convex deployment URL
# This is automatically created when you run `bunx convex dev`
# DO NOT manually set this - let Convex generate it
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=https://your-deployment.convex.cloud

# =============================================================================
# CLERK (https://dashboard.clerk.com)
# =============================================================================

# From Clerk Dashboard → API keys
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...

# Keep kit routes; Clerk path-based components use these
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/login
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=/signup
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_FALLBACK_REDIRECT_URL=/dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_FALLBACK_REDIRECT_URL=/dashboard

# =============================================================================
# CONVEX ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (Set via `bunx convex env set`)
# =============================================================================

# Clerk Frontend API URL / JWT issuer domain (same value)
# From https://dashboard.clerk.com/apps/setup/convex
# Dev format: https://verb-noun-00.clerk.accounts.dev
# Command: bunx convex env set CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN https://your-clerk-frontend-api-url
# CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN=https://verb-noun-00.clerk.accounts.dev

# =============================================================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# =============================================================================

# 1. Copy this file to .env.local:
#    cp .env.example .env.local

# 2. Create a Clerk app at https://dashboard.clerk.com/apps/new
#    Enable the Convex integration at https://dashboard.clerk.com/apps/setup/convex
#    Copy publishable + secret keys into .env.local

# 3. Run Convex dev (creates NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL):
#    bunx convex dev

# 4. Set the Clerk issuer on Convex:
#    bunx convex env set CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN https://your-clerk-frontend-api-url

# 5. Start the app:
#    bun run dev

# =============================================================================
# PRODUCTION
# =============================================================================

# Use production Clerk keys and issuer domain for prod deployments.
# bunx convex env set CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN https://clerk.your-domain.com --prod
# Set NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL and Clerk keys in your host (e.g. Vercel).

# =============================================================================
# NOTES
# =============================================================================

# - Never commit .env.local to git (it's in .gitignore)
# - Use different Clerk instances/keys for development and production
# - Convex env variables live in Convex cloud, not in .env.local
# - Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are exposed to the browser
# - See docs/AUTHENTICATION.md for the full Clerk + Convex flow
